   "en": "§ The Gemara returns to an analysis of a passage in the mishna. When one party takes possession of «an asimon,» the other party «acquires the» minted «coin.» The Gemara asks: «What» is «an asimon? Rav said:» It is one of the «coins given as a token» to gain entry «into the bathhouse,» for which the bathers would pay later."
